  "label": "Datasheet",
  "description": "Warm technical paper with an ink-blue rule. Every entry slide is the same form filled in: a counter chip, a dashed wire from your tool to the thing it reaches, a brand tile, then three fixed fields \u2014 what it does, why it's useful, and a numbered setup recipe in a dashed box. The recipe is the payload, so the deck is a save rather than a scroll. Built for integration and connector round-ups where each entry needs instructions, not a statistic. Animates: the fields land in reading order and the recipe steps type in. Derived from the DcSlXDIE2WD reference deck.",
